From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:43:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] xen: QEMU_XEN_IOREQ_FIFO runs the ioreq thread at SCHED_FIFO

The ioreq thread (q11-052/054) answers a guest vCPU's virtio-pci notify
writes and ISR reads, and queues the rest for the main loop. A vCPU
waits on it, but it ran at the device model's SCHED_OTHER nice value
beside the H.264 decoder's frame threads and the main loop, and waited
for a CPU behind them. QEMU_XEN_IOREQ_FIFO=N (1-99) has the thread set
itself to SCHED_FIFO priority N when it starts; unset or empty changes
nothing, and a value outside 1-99 is reported and ignored.

It cannot hold a CPU for long: it only polls the event channel and
answers or queues. On a Raspberry Pi 5 (2026-10-27, H.264 1080p60
played in a WebView) DomA's ioreq thread woke 398-422 times a second
and ran 27 ms a second.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [this layer's q11 ioreq thread]
---
 hw/xen/xen-hvm-common.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/xen/xen-hvm-common.c b/hw/xen/xen-hvm-common.c
index 872c1ce01..9c7f65b7b 100644
--- a/hw/xen/xen-hvm-common.c
+++ b/hw/xen/xen-hvm-common.c
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@
 #include "qemu/event_notifier.h"
 #include "qemu/rcu.h"
 #include <poll.h>
+#include <sched.h>          /* SCHED_FIFO, for QEMU_XEN_IOREQ_FIFO */
+#include "qemu/cutils.h"   /* qemu_strtoul */
 
 MemoryRegion xen_memory, xen_grants;
 
@@ -974,6 +976,37 @@ static void xen_ioreq_notified(void *opaque)
     g_free(it);
 }
 
+/*
+ * q11-xen-ioreq-fifo: QEMU_XEN_IOREQ_FIFO=N (1-99) runs the ioreq thread at SCHED_FIFO
+ * priority N, so that a guest vCPU waiting on an ioreq does not wait for a CPU behind
+ * the device model's other threads. The thread only polls the event channel and either
+ * answers or queues, a few hundred times a second for DomA (2026-10-27, Raspberry Pi 5,
+ * WebView 1080p60: 398-422 wakeups/s, 27 ms/s of CPU), so it cannot hold a CPU for long.
+ * Unset or empty leaves it at the device model's policy.
+ */
+static void xen_ioreq_thread_set_fifo(void)
+{
+    const char *e = getenv("QEMU_XEN_IOREQ_FIFO");
+    struct sched_param sp = { 0 };
+    unsigned long n;
+    int r;
+
+    if (!e || !*e) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (qemu_strtoul(e, NULL, 10, &n) < 0 || n < 1 || n > 99) {
+        warn_report("xen: QEMU_XEN_IOREQ_FIFO=%s is not 1-99; ignored", e);
+        return;
+    }
+    sp.sched_priority = (int)n;
+    r = pthread_setschedparam(pthread_self(), SCHED_FIFO, &sp);
+    if (r) {
+        warn_report("xen: ioreq thread: SCHED_FIFO %lu: %s", n, strerror(r));
+        return;
+    }
+    info_report("xen: ioreq thread at SCHED_FIFO %lu", n);
+}
+
 static void *xen_ioreq_thread(void *opaque)
 {
     XenIOState *state = opaque;
@@ -983,6 +1016,7 @@ static void *xen_ioreq_thread(void *opaque)
     int64_t last = qemu_clock_get_ms(QEMU_CLOCK_REALTIME);
 
     rcu_register_thread();
+    xen_ioreq_thread_set_fifo();
     for (;;) {
         struct pollfd pfd = { .fd = fd, .events = POLLIN };
         evtchn_port_t port;
-- 
